>> title: Hungarian Goulash, Instant Pot
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, paprika, hungarian, one-pot, stew, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> dish: hungarian-goulash
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> aka: gulyás, gulyas, beef goulash, instant pot goulash, pressure cooker goulash
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 35 min
>> slack: narrow — paprika burns against a hot base in about thirty seconds, and under a locked lid nobody sees it happen
>> washing-up: the Instant Pot

The paprika goes in with the pot switched off onto onions that have already given up their water.

>> step: render the onions 15 min, deep golden
Render @lard{2%Tbs}, @yellow onions{2%lb}(900 g; thinly sliced) on sauté in an #Instant Pot{} for ~render{15%min}, until deep golden and collapsed.

>> step: bloom the paprika off the heat
Bloom @Hungarian sweet paprika{1/4%cup}(30 g), @caraway seed{1%tsp}, @garlic{4%cloves}(minced) in @&(~1)onions{} with the heat switched off.

>> step: stir the beef in
Stir @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 1-in cubes), @kosher salt{1%Tbs} into @&(~1)paprika base{} until every cube is coated.

>> step: 35 min high pressure, natural release 15 min
Pressure cook @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{2%cup}(475 mL), @tomato{1%large}(chopped), @green pepper{1}(chopped), lid on and valve sealed: ~come to pressure{12%min}, then ~pressure cook{35%min} on high and ~natural release{15%min}.

>> step: add the potatoes, 4 min, quick release
Add @Yukon Gold potatoes{1%lb}(450 g; cut in 1-in cubes) to @&(~1)goulash{}, seal it again for ~pressure cook{4%min} on high, and ~quick release{2%min} at the beep.
